internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json:3201:      "gap": "Section 17.2 carries exactly one scanner-visible obligation, clause 17.2#1: a reader MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from it. That clause binds Session Event history, and Read classifies one completed CLI invocation rather than retaining any event, so this binding discharges none of Section 17.2's measured obligations. The four numbered reader rules the section states carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are therefore invisible to the clause scanner; three of them are implemented and tested here - Read and Decode settle the schema and major before any other member, the closed member set included, acceptsVersion implements the same-or-lower-minor rule, and an unknown namespaced extension survives a decode and re-encode byte for byte - while the unknown ownership/security enum rule is covered only for the closed CLI Result vocabularies, not for any lease or security enum, because no ownership implementation exists in this repository."
