LOGBOOK.md:827:- FINDING, the non-obvious half: an owner may be closed only once the scan passes strictly above `owner + "/"`, not on the first non-descendant path. `.` (0x2E) sorts below `/` (0x2F), so `a.txt` sits between `a` and `a/b`; the naive closing rule evicts the `a` owner before its escaping child arrives and admits the overlap. Mutant M5 is exactly that implementation and needed its own three-entry case to die.
